pretty_format() example<pre><code>data = {
    "name": "example",
    "values": [1, 2, 3],
    "nested": {
        "key": "value"
    }
}
print(snick.pretty_format(data))
</code></pre> output<pre><code>{
  'name': 'example',
  'values': [
    1,
    2,
    3,
  ],
  'nested': {
    'key': 'value',
  },
}
</code></pre> <p>It also works with types like <code>datetime</code>, <code>Decimal</code>, and custom classes:</p> pretty_format() with datetime and Decimal<pre><code>from datetime import datetime
from decimal import Decimal

data = {
    "timestamp": datetime(2026, 1, 22, 20, 15, 30),
    "amount": Decimal("123.45"),
    "active": True,
    "notes": None,
}
print(snick.pretty_format(data))
</code></pre> output<pre><code>{
  'timestamp': datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 22, 20, 15, 30),
  'amount': Decimal('123.45'),
  'active': True,
  'notes': None,
}
</code></pre>
